03:47:31.960 --> 03:47:34.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: will reportedly no longer be released,

asr-000892
03:47:34.960 --> 03:47:36.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: despite my efforts to approach

asr-000893
03:47:36.960 --> 03:47:38.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: various individuals and offices

asr-000894
03:47:38.960 --> 03:47:40.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: to seek assistance.

asr-000895
03:47:40.960 --> 03:47:42.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: After exhausting these efforts,

asr-000896
03:47:42.960 --> 03:47:44.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: I was informed that the funding

asr-000897
03:47:44.960 --> 03:47:46.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: will no longer materialize.

asr-000898
03:47:48.960 --> 03:47:50.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: This raises a serious question.

asr-000899
03:47:50.960 --> 03:47:52.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: What happens to the projects

asr-000900
03:47:52.960 --> 03:47:54.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: that were supposed to be implemented,

asr-000901
03:47:54.960 --> 03:47:56.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: and more importantly,

asr-000902
03:47:56.960 --> 03:47:58.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: to the constituents who were supposed

asr-000903
03:47:58.960 --> 03:48:00.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: to benefit from them?

asr-000904
03:48:00.960 --> 03:48:05.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: I vote no because another 642.958 million

asr-000905
03:48:05.960 --> 03:48:09.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: from our 2026 allocation remains unreleased.

asr-000906
03:48:09.960 --> 03:48:12.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: Our city deserves a clear accounting

asr-000907
03:48:12.960 --> 03:48:14.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: of these funds and an explanation

asr-000908
03:48:14.960 --> 03:48:16.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: for the delays.

asr-000909
03:48:16.960 --> 03:48:18.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: We need concrete answers regarding

asr-000910
03:48:18.960 --> 03:48:20.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: the status of the projects

asr-000911
03:48:20.960 --> 03:48:22.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: for which they were appropriated.

asr-000912
03:48:22.960 --> 03:48:25.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: I vote no because my district continues

asr-000913
03:48:25.960 --> 03:48:27.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: to suffer from recurring floods

asr-000914
03:48:27.960 --> 03:48:29.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: and our people urgently need

asr-000915
03:48:29.960 --> 03:48:31.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: efficient drainage systems,

asr-000916
03:48:31.960 --> 03:48:33.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: flood control infrastructures,

asr-000917
03:48:33.960 --> 03:48:35.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: improved waterways,

asr-000918
03:48:35.960 --> 03:48:37.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: and resilient public works.

asr-000919
03:48:37.960 --> 03:48:40.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: Flooding threatens homes,

asr-000920
03:48:40.960 --> 03:48:42.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: disrupts livelihoods,

asr-000921
03:48:42.960 --> 03:48:44.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: damages properties,

asr-000922
03:48:44.960 --> 03:48:46.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: and puts lives at risk.

asr-000923
03:48:46.960 --> 03:48:49.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: These are not optional projects.

asr-000924
03:48:49.960 --> 03:48:51.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: They are essential investments

asr-000925
03:48:51.960 --> 03:48:54.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: in public safety, economic security,

asr-000926
03:48:54.960 --> 03:48:56.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: and human dignity.

asr-000927
03:48:56.960 --> 03:48:58.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: How can we adequately protect

asr-000928
03:48:58.960 --> 03:49:01.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: our constituents from recurring floods

asr-000929
03:49:01.960 --> 03:49:03.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: when funding for critical infrastructure

asr-000930
03:49:03.960 --> 03:49:05.220
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: remains uncertain

asr-000931
03:49:05.220 --> 03:49:08.500
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: and our proposed allocation continues to shrink?

asr-000932
03:49:09.940 --> 03:49:12.200
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: I vote no because a substantial

asr-000933
03:49:12.200 --> 03:49:14.020
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: reduction in our district's

asr-000934
03:49:14.020 --> 03:49:15.160
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: infrastructure allocation

asr-000935
03:49:15.740 --> 03:49:17.480
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: raises serious questions

asr-000936
03:49:17.480 --> 03:49:19.320
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: about whether the proposed budget

asr-000937
03:49:19.320 --> 03:49:21.040
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: adequately addresses the needs

asr-000938
03:49:21.040 --> 03:49:21.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: of our people.

asr-000939
03:49:21.960 --> 03:49:23.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: As a highly urbanized city

asr-000940
03:49:23.960 --> 03:49:25.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: facing recurring and severe flooding,

asr-000941
03:49:25.960 --> 03:49:27.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: we require sustained investments

asr-000942
03:49:27.960 --> 03:49:29.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: in drainage systems,

asr-000943
03:49:29.960 --> 03:49:31.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: flood control facilities,

asr-000944
03:49:31.960 --> 03:49:32.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: waterways,

asr-000945
03:49:32.960 --> 03:49:34.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: and other critical infrastructure.

asr-000946
03:49:34.960 --> 03:49:36.960
Rep. Rachel Marguerite B. Del Mar: Budgetary investments

asr-000947
03:49:36.960 --> 03:49:38.960
